% Generate `tools/audio/audio_mixer.py`: an `AudioMixer(BaseTool)` that wraps FFmpeg
% (and optionally pydub) to mix speech/music/SFX with ducking, fades, normalization,
% loudness auto-balancing, and audio extraction. FFmpeg-only mode works without pydub.
% `from __future__ import annotations`. Import math, re, time, `pathlib.Path`,
% typing `Any, Optional`, and from `tools.base_tool`: BaseTool, Determinism,
% ExecutionMode, ResourceProfile, ToolResult, ToolStability, ToolStatus, ToolTier.
%
% Module docstring must record these documented limitations (they are load-bearing —
% each fixes a live-verified bug):
%   - Per-track fades apply to the SOURCE audio BEFORE any start_seconds delay, so
%     fade_in ramps the real start and fade_out lands on the real end. fade_out emits
%     an explicit afade st= from the probed duration (FFmpeg defaults st=0, which fades
%     the FIRST N seconds to silence and keeps the track muted).
%   - auto_balance measures integrated LUFS per track and gains toward a voice-anchored
%     target. In apply mode amix scales each input by 1/n, so relative balance is
%     preserved but absolute level may sit below target — run normalize=true for
%     delivery loudness. Gains capped at +/-30 dB.
%   - extract defaults are UNCHANGED (pcm_s16le 16kHz mono, transcription grade);
%     pass codec for full-fidelity detach.
%
% BaseTool provides `run_command(cmd, *, timeout, cwd)` (subprocess.run, capture_output,
% text, check=True — non-zero exit RAISES CalledProcessError) and the ToolResult dataclass
% (success, data, artifacts, error, duration_seconds). Do NOT re-implement them.

## Class metadata
name "audio_mixer", version "0.2.0", tier CORE, capability "audio_processing",
provider "ffmpeg", stability EXPERIMENTAL, execution_mode SYNC, determinism DETERMINISTIC.
`dependencies = ["cmd:ffmpeg"]`; install_instructions notes FFmpeg required + optional
`pip install pydub`; `agent_skills = ["ffmpeg", "video_toolkit"]`.
`capabilities = ["mix","duck","fade","normalize","extract_audio","segmented_music","auto_balance"]`.
`not_good_for`: HDR sources — output is 8-bit SDR; detect via is_hdr_source() and handle
HDR per AGENT_GUIDE before use.
`resource_profile = ResourceProfile(cpu_cores=2, ram_mb=1024, vram_mb=0, disk_mb=500)`;
`idempotency_key_fields = ["operation","tracks","ducking"]`;
`side_effects = ["writes mixed audio file to output_path"]`;
`user_visible_verification` = listen and verify speech clarity + music ducking.

Class constants:
- `ROLE_ALIASES` maps voice/speech/primary→"voice", music/secondary→"music", sfx→"sfx".
- `MAX_BALANCE_GAIN_DB = 30.0`.
- `EXTRACT_CODECS` maps codec→(ffmpeg encoder, default ext): copy→(None,None),
  aac→("aac",".m4a"), wav & pcm_s16le→("pcm_s16le",".wav"), mp3→("libmp3lame",".mp3").
- `COPY_EXT_BY_CODEC` maps a probed source codec to a container ext:
  aac→.m4a, mp3→.mp3, opus & vorbis→.ogg, flac→.flac, ac3→.ac3, eac3→.eac3.

## input_schema
JSON-schema object, required `["operation"]`. `operation` enum:
mix, duck, extract, full_mix, segmented_music, auto_balance — with a description of each
(mix = layer tracks; duck = lower music under speech; extract = pull audio from video;
full_mix = narration+music ducked+normalized in one call, preferred for compose-director;
segmented_music = music into a video only during given time windows; auto_balance =
LUFS-match voice/music/sfx toward targets, dry-run or mix). Properties (all documented):
- `tracks`: array of `{path, role, volume(0–1, default 1.0), start_seconds, fade_in_seconds,
  fade_out_seconds}`, role enum speech/music/sfx/primary/secondary/voice.
- Simple duck: `primary_audio`, `secondary_audio`, `duck_level` (dB, default -12).
- extract: `input_path`, `codec` (enum copy/aac/wav/pcm_s16le/mp3), `sample_rate`(int≥1),
  `channels`(int≥1), `stream_index`(int≥0).
- auto_balance: `target_lufs_voice`(default -16), `music_offset_db`(default -12),
  `sfx_offset_db`(default -8), `apply`(bool default True; false = dry run).
- `ducking` object: enabled(default True), music_volume_during_speech(0–1 default 0.15),
  attack_ms(default 200), release_ms(default 500).
- `normalize`(bool default True), `output_path`.
- segmented_music: `video_path`, `music_path`, `music_volume`(0–1 default 0.20),
  `segments` array of `{start,end}`, `fade_duration`(default 0.5).

## execute
Read operation, start a timer, dispatch to `_mix/_duck/_extract/_full_mix/_segmented_music/
_auto_balance`; unknown → failure ToolResult. Wrap the dispatch in try/except: catch
`_MixInputError` and any Exception → `ToolResult(success=False, error=str(e))`. Set
`result.duration_seconds = round(elapsed, 2)` and return.

## Operations
All operations `mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` the output parent, validate that every
input path exists (failure ToolResult naming the missing file), and return
`artifacts=[output_path]` on success with a `data` dict that includes `"operation"`.
Default output names: mix→mixed_audio.wav, duck→ducked_audio.wav, full_mix→
full_mix_output.wav, auto_balance→auto_balanced_audio.wav, segmented_music→
segmented_music_output.mp4.

### `_mix`
Fail if no tracks. Build `-i path` per track and one `_per_track_chain(i, track)` filter per
track, then amix all into `[mixed]`: `...amix=inputs=N:duration=longest:dropout_transition=2`.
If normalize: append `[mixed]loudnorm=I=-16:LRA=11:TP=-1.5[out]` and map `[out]`, else map
`[mixed]`. Run via `_run`; on error return `mix failed: {err}`. data has track_count,
output, normalized.

### `_duck`
Resolve a speech path and a music path from EITHER format:
- Simple: `primary_audio`/`secondary_audio`. If `duck_level` is given and no explicit
  `ducking`, convert dB→linear (`10**(db/20)`, round 4) and set it as
  `music_volume_during_speech` on a COPY of the ducking dict (don't mutate the caller).
- Advanced `tracks`: first track with role in {speech,primary} = speech, first in
  {music,secondary} = music (only when the simple keys were absent).
Fail if either path is unresolved (message explaining both input formats). Then
`music_vol = ducking.music_volume_during_speech (0.15)`, `attack = attack_ms(200)/1000`,
`release = release_ms(500)/1000` — NOTE this op passes attack/release in SECONDS. Filter:
`[1:a]sidechaincompress=threshold=0.02:ratio=9:attack={attack}:release={release}:level_sc=1:
mix=0.9[ducked];[ducked]volume={music_vol*3}[music_out];[0:a][music_out]amix=inputs=2:
duration=longest[out]`. Run with `run_command` (raises on failure → caught by execute).
data has speech_track, music_track, output.

### `_extract`
Pull audio from a video; the no-codec default is UNCHANGED for back-compat. Validate first
(all pure, no ffmpeg): unknown codec → error listing EXTRACT_CODECS; sample_rate/channels
must be positive ints (reject bool); stream_index must be a non-negative int (reject bool);
codec=="copy" with sample_rate/channels → error (copy can't resample). Fail if input missing.
Resolve encoder/ext:
- codec is None → legacy: acodec pcm_s16le, ext .wav, default sample_rate 16000, channels 1.
- codec=="copy" → probe source codec (`_probe_audio_codec`); none found → fail; acodec "copy",
  ext from COPY_EXT_BY_CODEC (fallback `.wav` if source starts with `pcm_`, else `.mka`).
- else acodec,ext from EXTRACT_CODECS.
output defaults to input with the resolved suffix. cmd: `ffmpeg -y -i input -vn`, add
`-map 0:a:{stream_index}` when given, `-acodec {acodec}`, and when not copy add `-ar`/`-ac`
if set. Run via `_run`; also fail if the output is missing or zero bytes. data: input,
output, `codec` (source codec when copying else acodec), plus stream_copied=True when
copying, and echo sample_rate/channels/stream_index when they were set.

### `_auto_balance`
Fail if no tracks. `target_voice = target_lufs_voice(-16)`; targets voice=target_voice,
music=target_voice+music_offset_db(-12), sfx=target_voice+sfx_offset_db(-8). Normalize each
track's role through ROLE_ALIASES (unknown role → error); missing path → error. For each,
measure integrated LUFS (`_measure_lufs`; None → error), `gain_db = target - measured`, cap
its magnitude at MAX_BALANCE_GAIN_DB (flag `gain_capped` when clamped), `volume =
round(10**(gain_db/20), 6)`. Build a `report` entry (path, role, measured_lufs, target_lufs,
gain_db, volume — all rounded) and a mix-track carrying volume + any start/fade fields.
data: targets_lufs (rounded), tracks=report, applied. If `apply` is false, return data now
(no file, no artifacts). Otherwise call `_mix` with the computed tracks and
`normalize=inputs.get("normalize", False)` (default OFF — a post-mix loudnorm would
re-target and obscure the balance); on mix failure return it; else copy output/normalized
into data and return with mix artifacts.

### `_full_mix`
One-call mix preferred by compose-director. Fail if no tracks. Partition into speech
({speech,primary}), music ({music,secondary}), sfx ({sfx}); order = speech+music+sfx; fail
if empty. Validate files. Build `-i` + `_per_track_chain` per track (indices follow that
order). Ducking enabled = `ducking.enabled` (default True) when ducking is a dict else its
truthiness.
- If duck-enabled AND both speech and music exist: mix the speech tracks to `[speech_all]`
  (amix if >1 else `anull`), then `[speech_all]asplit=2[speech_key][speech_out]` — the speech
  signal is needed BOTH as the sidechain key and in the final mix, and an ffmpeg pad is
  consumable only once (consuming it multiple times left an orphan pad and errored). Mix the
  music tracks to `[music_all]` the same way. attack/release come from
  `attack_ms`(default 20)/`release_ms`(default 250) clamped to [0.01, 2000] and passed in
  MILLISECONDS (do NOT divide — a prior /1000 fell below the 0.01 floor and broke the graph).
  `[music_all][speech_key]sidechaincompress=threshold=0.02:ratio=9:attack=..:release=..:
  level_sc=1:mix=0.9[ducked_music];[ducked_music]volume={music_vol*3}[music_out]`
  (music_vol default 0.15). Final `amix` of `[speech_out][music_out]` + any sfx pads
  (inputs=2+n_sfx) → `[premix]`.
- Else: amix all tracks with `duration=longest:dropout_transition=2` → `[premix]`.
Then normalize (loudnorm as in `_mix`) mapping `[out]` else `[premix]`. Join filter parts
skipping empties. Run via `_run`. data: per-role counts, ducking_enabled, normalized, output.

### `_segmented_music`
Mix music into a video only inside given time windows, silent elsewhere. Fail on missing
video/music/segments. ffprobe the video duration (`format=duration`, first line). For each
segment sorted by start, build a piecewise volume expression over t: 0 before start,
linear ramp up over `fade_duration`, hold at `music_volume`, linear ramp down over the last
`fade_duration`, 0 after end. Sum the per-segment expressions (parenthesized) if more than
one. Filter: loop/trim the music `[1:a]atrim=0:{dur},asetpts=PTS-STARTPTS,volume='{expr}':
eval=frame[music_shaped]`, aformat both the video audio `[0:a]` and the shaped music to
fltp/44100/stereo, then `amix=inputs=2:duration=first:dropout_transition=2[aout]`. cmd:
`ffmpeg -y -i video -stream_loop -1 -i music -filter_complex .. -map 0:v -map [aout]
-c:v copy -c:a aac -b:a 192k output`. Run with `run_command`; fail if no output produced.
data echoes video, music, segments, music_volume, fade_duration, output.

## Helpers
`_per_track_chain(index, track) -> str` — build `[index:a]<filters>[a{index}]`, or
`[index:a]acopy[a{index}]` when there are no filters. In order: if `duration_seconds`>0,
`atrim=0:{dur},asetpts=PTS-STARTPTS` (truncate to a window LENGTH first); `volume={v}` when
volume != 1.0; `afade=t=in:st=0:d={fade_in}` when fade_in>0; for fade_out>0 compute
`base_dur` = the trim length if trimmed else `_audio_duration(path)` (None → raise
`_MixInputError`), `st = max(0.0, round(base_dur - fade_out, 3))`, `afade=t=out:st={st}:
d={fade_out}`; finally `adelay={ms}|{ms}` (ms = int(start_seconds*1000)) when >0 — adelay is
ALWAYS last so fades act on the audio, not the silence pad.

`_audio_duration(path) -> Optional[float]` — ffprobe `format=duration` (timeout 30); first
line, None on "N/A"/empty or on CalledProcessError/TimeoutExpired/ValueError.

`_measure_lufs(path) -> Optional[float]` — run `ffmpeg -hide_banner -nostats -i path -vn -af
ebur128 -f null -` (timeout 600); from stderr take the text after the last `"Summary:"`,
regex `I:\s*(-?(?:\d+(?:\.\d+)?|inf))\s+LUFS`; None if unmatched or "inf" (live per-frame
lines also print `I:`, so only the final summary counts).

`_probe_audio_codec(path, stream_index=None) -> Optional[str]` — ffprobe
`stream=codec_name` for `a:{stream_index or 0}` (timeout 30); first line or None.

`_run(cmd) -> Optional[str]` — run_command(timeout 900): None on success; catch
CalledProcessError → the stderr tail `[-500:]` (or "ffmpeg failed"); TimeoutExpired →
"ffmpeg timed out." (BaseTool.run_command uses check=True, so failures raise rather than
returning a code.)

Module-level `class _MixInputError(Exception)` — bad audio-op parameters, validated before
any ffmpeg spend.

